# Cousins articles

A cousin page is one **melody** with many lives. Chrome matches History.
Details and the honesty rules live in `docs/plans/cousins-module.md`.

## Copy standard — do not invent titles or link labels

House phrasing is locked. Import the helpers from
`src/lib/cousins/registry.ts`. Do **not** write “Where else does this
tune live?”, “This tune also lives as…”, or a custom search-question
per article (Dona Dona used to; that is retired).

| Surface | Copy | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Hub `<h1>` / nav label | **Cousins** | keep |
| Hub tagline / nav description | **One melody, many lives** | `COUSIN_SONG_HEADING` |
| Song-page section heading | **One melody, many lives** | `COUSIN_SONG_HEADING` |
| Song-page card (one cousin) | **History & versions** | `cousinSongLinkLabel` |
| Song-page card (several) | **{name} — history & versions** | `cousinSongLinkLabel` |
| Spoke `<h1>`, `<title>`, FAQ, RelatedPages, search title, inline “see also” | **History & versions of {name}** | `cousinQuestion(name)` — derived; never stored |
| Hub card CTA | **History & versions** | `COUSIN_SONG_LINK` |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — old “live” metaphor, or a one-off question
question: "Where else does Misirlou live?"
<h2>This tune also lives as…</h2>
<Link href="/cousins/dona-dona">Where else does Dona Dona live?</Link>

// ✅ GOOD — helpers only
import {
  COUSIN_SONG_HEADING,
  cousinQuestion,
  cousinSongLinkLabel,
} from "@/lib/cousins/registry";

<h2>{COUSIN_SONG_HEADING}</h2>
label={cousinSongLinkLabel(cousin, cousins.length)}
<Link href="/cousins/miserlou">{cousinQuestion("Misirlou")}</Link>
```

A new registry row has `name` only. `publishCousin` sets `question`.
Do not add a `question` field to a draft.

## Ship checklist

1. Registry row in `src/lib/cousins/registry.ts` — `genres` is **required**
   (existing genre slugs only; don't invent "rebetiko" / "surf").
2. Body in `src/content/cousins/<Name>.tsx` (server TSX) +
   `src/content/cousins/index.ts`.
3. Every named recording is a `CatalogSong` **and** a `members[]` row.
4. That song lists `cousins: ["<this-slug>"]`. Both sides, same change.
5. `<GenrePills>` on the hub card and the spoke header (empty `genres` is a bug).
6. **`places` — every place the body names, accurately** (see below).
7. **Loanwords + pronunciation — every non-English word** (see below).
8. No lyric blocks here — link `/songs/<slug>`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — song named in prose, not a member, no reverse field
members: [{ song: "misirlou-dale", kind: "rearrangement" }]
// songs.ts: misirlou-dale has no cousins: []

// ✅ GOOD — both directions
// cousins registry: members: [{ song: "misirlou-dale", kind: "rearrangement" }]
// songs.ts: cousins: ["miserlou"], genres: ["rock"]  // when a slug fits
```

## Places — map the whole journey, accurately

The spoke's `<PageMapSection>` reads `article.places` verbatim. A one-city
list is almost always **wrong**: a tune that traveled touches several places.

- List **every place the body cites** — origin, each rearrangement/translation
  home, each performer's base — as place-registry ids.
- Only pin what the prose actually supports; kinship-by-vibe is not a place.
- If a cited place is missing from `src/lib/places/registry.ts`, **add it**
  (sourced blurb) in the same change, then reference it. Don't shrink the map
  because the registry is thin.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — story spans Poland, New York, Israel; map shows one dot
places: ["new-york"]
// ✅ GOOD — every cited home
places: ["poland", "new-york", "israel"]
```

## Loanwords + pronunciation — always both

Every word from another language in the body (song titles, refrains, vocables,
dance names) gets a `SpokenWord` in `src/lib/words/registry.ts` with a verified
native spelling, wrapped on first mention with `<Word>` (or `<Term>` if it's
also a concept).

- **Always hunt for a speaker.** Follow `.cursor/rules/pronunciation-audio.mdc`:
  real human clip, matching word/sense, openly licensed → self-host + credit.
  New language → add its table row there. No clip → no speaker, and record the
  search so the next agent doesn't repeat it.
- Latin-script languages (Polish, Romanian) still earn an entry — the value is
  the **speaker**, not a native parenthetical.
- Keep `latin`/`aliases` specific so the auto-linker can't false-match (a bare
  `"dana"` would grab "Dana, Dana, Dana" in a bio; scope it to `"oj, dana dana"`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — foreign refrain left as plain italics: no home spelling, no speaker
<em>oj, dana dana</em>
// ✅ GOOD — registered word + hunted, licensed clip
<Word id="oj-dana"><em>oj, dana dana</em></Word>
```

## Song page reverse

The song page shows **`COUSIN_SONG_HEADING`** (each link from
**`cousinSongLinkLabel`**) at the **top** (under title / genre pills).
`getCousinsBySong` unions members + `song.cousins`;
still fix drift so they match.

Kinship is a cited claim. Same mode ≠ cousins.
